        {
            "structure": {
                "para": [
                    {
                        "id": "75",
                        "text": "Step 5"
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "76",
                        "text": "5. Give brief details of your findings or results."
                    }
                ]
            },
            "notes": {
                "para": []
            },
            "content": {
                "para": [
                    [
                        {
                            "id": "78",
                            "text": " Measurements of the filtration properties indicate that these membranes have a high retention rate in removing bacteria (‘Escherichia coli’, hereafter referred to as ‘E. coli’) and viruses (MS2 bacteriophage) in water, while maintaining high flux permeation. "
                        }
                    ]
                ],
                "placeHolder": "Type Step 5 here.",
                "id": "77"
            }
        },
        {
            "structure": {
                "para": [
                    {
                        "id": "80",
                        "text": "Steps 6 and 7"
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "81",
                        "text": "6. Justify your research by showing the significance or contribution of your study.\n</br>7. Describe briefly the organization of your dissertation."
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "82",
                        "text": "TIP Step 7 is optional, but likely to be included in a full dissertation, where the Introduction is a complete chapter.",
                        "tip": true
                    }
                ]
            },
            "notes": {
                "para": []
            },
            "content": {
                "para": [
                    [
                        {
                            "id": "84",
                            "text": " High-resolution electron microscopy investigations revealed, for the first time, the detailed nanoscale fibrous networks in membranes that are responsible for these superior filtration properties. "
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "85",
                            "text": " The demonstrated membrane system opens a door to the further development of other nanostructured biomaterials to adsorb water pathogens and contaminants and increases the realization of the much needed inexpensive MF membranes. "
                        }
                    ],
                    [
                        {
                            "id": "83",
                            "text": " (Sato et al., 2011) For the full reference, see "
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "83",
                            "text": "<a href=\"/references\">References</a>"
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "83",
                            "text": "."
                        }
                    ]
                ],
                "placeHolder": "Type Steps 6 and 7 here.",
                "id": "83"
